2026-01-09 13:17:43 - claude-primitive-finder - INFO - Claude thinks: Let me analyze this vulnerability and develop an exploit to achieve shell execution.

## Understanding the Vulnerability

The vulnerability is in QuickJS's `Atomics` operations. When performing atomic operations on TypedArrays backed by resizable ArrayBuffers:

1. A pointer to the buffer element is captured early
2. User code can execute via `valueOf()` callbacks when converting the value argument
3. This user code can resize the underlying ArrayBuffer
4. The stale pointer is then used for the atomic operation

This gives us either:
- Use-after-free (if buffer was moved to new memory)
- Out-of-bounds read/write (if buffer was shrunk in-place)

Let me start by understanding the codebase and heap behavior with the real allocator.
